Hey team, I'd like to clarify some aspects of the current process as the problem has been described inaccurately.

The current process is as follows:

a) Leads that register with *their delivery bags* - deposit is not taken; 

b) Leads that register without a bag are offered to use our Bag  (BF). We inform them that, in this case, a deposit will be taken;

c) Ex-courier-partner registering with us again, who did not return our bag (we still hold his deposit) - we reactivate his old account (if possible) *and do not take a second deposit*;

d) If a lead registers with someone else's BF bag that was not returned to us, we deduct the deposit from the lead, explaining that it is our property. We return the deposit to the bag owner (ex-courier) if they contact us. This process is not automated, as in 9 out of 10 cases, the bag owner did not return the bag, as they chose to sell it at a higher price on the marketplace - which is forbidden. 

With this process in place - we don't charge a courier partner twice. 

However, if this is deemed a legal issue, please inform us. In that case, a deposit won't be taken from leads who register with someone else's Bolt Food bag.

